The function starts when you call `dataProcessor.start()` and stops when you call `dataProcessor.stop()`. There's also a mechanism for pausing and resuming the service, though it needs further implementation to dynamically adjust the frequency based on current system load and resource availability.

To customize the behavior of the DataProcessor, you can modify the configuration file (e.g., `config.json`) containing the service configurations. You may also want to add monitoring and logging for tracking performance metrics and operational states. This implementation is scalable and supports easy integration with existing infrastructure."]

