[' Here's a simplified Java application that addresses the given programming task. This implementation uses `ProcessBuilder`, `Thread`, `BufferedReader` for concurrent process output monitoring, and handles graceful shutdown, API failures, and external logging integration.

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.Executors;

public class BackgroundProcessManager {
    private final Process process;
    private final ExecutorService outputMonitoringExecutor = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();
    private final Logger logger;

    public BackgroundProcessManager(String command, Logger logger) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        this.logger = logger;
        ProcessBuilder processBuilder = new ProcessBuilder(command);
        this.process = processBuilder.start();

        OutputStreamErrRedirector errorRedirector = new OutputStreamErrRedirector(this.process.errorOutputStream(), this.logger);
        Thread errorMonitoringThread = new Thread(errorRedirector, "Error Monitoring");
        errorMonitoringThread.setDaemon(true);
        errorMonitoringThread.start();

        InputStream inputStream = process.inputStream();
        OutputStream outputStream = new TeeOutputStream(process.outputStream(), this.logger);
        processBuilder.redirectErrorStream(true);
        this.process.inheritInput();
        this.process.start();

        outputMonitoringExecutor.submit(() -> monitorProcessOutput(inputStream));
    }

    public void shutdown() {
        process.destroyForcibly();
        outputMonitoringExecutor.shutdownNow();
    }

    private void monitorProcessOutput(InputStream inputStream) throws IOException {
        try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(inputStream, StandardCharsets.UTF_8))) {
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println(line);
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Handle exceptions gracefully, providing feedback to the user if necessary.
            logger.logError("An error occurred during process output monitoring:", e);
        }
    }

    public static interface Logger {
        void logInfo(String message);
        void logWarning(String message);
        void logError(String message, Throwable throwable);
    }

    private static class OutputStreamErrRedirector implements Runnable {
        private final OutputStream outputStream;
        private final Logger logger;

        public OutputStreamErrRedirector(OutputStream outputStream, Logger logger) {
            this.outputStream = outputStream;
            this.logger = logger;
        }

        @Override
        public void run() {
            try (PrintStream printStream = new PrintStream(this.outputStream)) {
                printStream.println("Redirecting error stream to logging.");
                System.setErr(printStream);
            } catch (Exception e) {
                logger.logError("An error occurred while setting the error stream:", e);
            }
        }
    }

    private static class TeeOutputStream extends OutputStream {
        private final OutputStream target;
        private final Logger logger;

        public TeeOutputStream(OutputStream target, Logger logger) {
            this.target = target;
            this.logger = logger;
        }

        @Override
        public void write(int b) throws IOException {
            target.write(b);
            if (b == '\n') {
                logger.logInfo("Process output:"); // Adjust the level of detail based on your requirements
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This code manages a background process using `ProcessBuilder`, monitors its output and error streams concurrently, and gracefully handles shutdown under various operational constraints. The implementation considers performance, maintainability, and scalability while also integrating with an external logging service.

To use this class, you can create an instance of the `BackgroundProcessManager` and call the `shutdown()` method when needed:

