The class is optimized for memory usage and minimizes garbage collection overhead during high load conditions. Concurrency is handled using a lock-free approach for reading data from the CryptoStream, which is more efficient than thread-safe mechanisms when handling large volumes of data concurrently. The function dynamically adjusts its behavior based on current load conditions by adapting to different execution strategies for better resource utilization.

Comprehensive unit tests cover a wide range of scenarios, including malformed inputs, performance bottlenecks under high load, and edge cases. These tests focus on both correctness and efficiency to ensure the function meets performance goals without sacrificing reliability. Memory leaks are managed by properly disposing of temporary structures during decryption.

The implementation takes into account the impact of different garbage collection strategies on overall performance and adapts accordingly to optimize for the specific environment where the service will operate.']

