["```javascript
class FileJSONManager {
  constructor(baseDir, logger) {
    this.baseDir = baseDir;
    this.schemas = {};
    this.factories = new Map();
    this.cache = new Map();
    this.logger = logger;
  }

  async readJSON(path) {
    if (!this.cache.has(path)) {
      try {
        const fileContent = await fs.promises.readFile(`${this.baseDir}/${path}.json`, 'utf8');
        this.cache.set(path, JSON.parse(fileContent));
        return this.cache.get(path);
      } catch (error) {
        if (error.code === 'ENOENT') {
          this.logger.error(`File not found: ${path}`);
        } else {
          this.logger.error(`Error reading file: ${path}, error: ${error}`);
        }
      }
    }
    return this.cache.get(path);
  }

  async writeJSON(path, data) {
    const jsonData = JSON.stringify(data, null, 2);
    try {
      await fs.promises.writeFile(`${this.baseDir}/${path}.json`, jsonData, 'utf8');
      this.cache.set(path, data);
    } catch (error) {
      this.logger.error(`Error writing file: ${path}, error: ${error}`);
    }
  }

  async discoverSchemas() {
    const schemaDir = `${this.baseDir}/schemas`;
    const files = await fs.promises.readdir(schemaDir, { withFileTypes: true });
    for (const file of files) {
      if (file.isFile()) {
        try {
          const schemaContent = await fs.promises.readFile(`${schemaDir}/${file.name}.json`, 'utf8');
          this.schemas[file.name] = JSON.parse(schemaContent);
        } catch (error) {
          this.logger.error(`Error reading schema file: ${file.name}, error: ${error}`);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  registerFactory(className, factoryFunction) {
    const id = factoryFunction.id;
    if (this.factories.has(id)) {
      this.logger.error(`Duplicate ID found while registering factory: ${id}`);
      return;
    }
    this.factories.set(id, { className, factoryFunction });
  }

  async createInstance(className, data) {
    const id = this.factories.get(className).factoryFunction.id;
    if (!data || !this.schemas[className]) {
      throw new Error('Invalid JSON data or missing schema');
    }

    let instanceData = data;
    for (const [schemaName, schema] of Object.entries(this.schemas)) {
      if (schemaName === className) continue;
      try {
        const isValid = await this.factories.get(className).factoryFunction.validator(data, schema);
        if (isValid) instanceData = data;
      } catch (error) {
        this.logger.error(`Error validating JSON data: ${error}`);
        continue;
      }
    }

    if (!instanceData) throw new Error('JSON data is invalid according to all registered schemas');

    const factory = this.factories.get(className);
    return new factory.className(instanceData);
  }
}
```

This code assumes the existence of `fs` module for file operations, and an external logger object with `error` method. The `FileJSONManager` class manages JSON data across multiple directories, supports asynchronous file operations, dynamically discovers available schema files within the directory structure, validates incoming JSON data against these schemas, registers custom factory functions for creating instances of subclasses, and provides functionality to handle errors related to missing or corrupted files, invalid JSON data, and conflicts when registering new factories. Performance optimizations are considered by caching frequently accessed files."]

