        shuffle($pool);
        return $pool;
    }

    public function generateToken(): string {
        if (empty($this->tokenPool)) {
            $this->tokenPool = $this->generateTokenPool();
        }
        return array_shift($this->tokenPool);
    }
}
```

This PHP class creates a scalable session token service. The `SessionTokenService` constructor initializes a token pool, and the `generateTokenPool()` method generates 1,000,000 unique tokens using base64 encoding of random bytes. Each time the `generateToken()` method is called, it returns a token from the pool or regenerates the pool if it's empty.

You can use this class in your web application to generate and manage session tokens. Ensure that you have proper caching and handling mechanisms for efficient performance in high-traffic scenarios."]

