The function `createArray(int N)` takes care of edge cases by ensuring that the input value for `N` is within the valid range (1 to 10,000). It also optimizes the performance under high load conditions by reusing memory from the pool whenever possible. The choice of a custom memory pool helps improve performance at the cost of increased complexity and potential code maintenance overhead.

