- Use C++11 features for concurrency and thread safety (std::atomic, std::queue, std::mutex).
- Implement a circular buffer (FrameBuffer) to manage the frames.
- Leverage multiple worker threads (FrameManager) to process frames concurrently.
- Abstract external data processing service as a callback function (processNetworkData) for flexibility and minimal latency impact.
- Update signal quality metrics based on received packet statistics (in the comment "Process the frame and update SQM here").
- Use locking mechanisms strategically to minimize lock contention (e.g., dequeue locks only while updating current_).
- Implement a graceful shutdown mechanism (FrameManager::stop()) for intermittent connectivity handling.']

