Randomly setting CRCFLAG in the constructor ensures that new structures have a unique value, while also accounting for variability in structure sizes due to different tags and tag values. The code handles potential discrepancies in data synchronization between different components of the system by checking for duplicate RTNIs and incrementing RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG if needed.

The system adapts dynamically to changes in the number of threads and data sources, as new structures are added to the list, and old ones are removed from the circular buffer when the maximum size is reached. The destructor handles memory deallocation efficiently, avoiding memory leaks.']

